From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:09:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sf_smac: do not overrun the RF gain table index arrays

The parser reads each index into an unsigned int and memcpy()s all four
bytes into a u8 array of four entries, so the last entry writes three
bytes past the end of lb_rf_gain_tb_idx or hb_rf_gain_tb_idx. Store the
value as a u8.

Found by fortify on the Banana Pi BPI-WiFi5, together with the same
defect in the tx-power gain table parser, which already reads into a u8
on this branch.

This is the fix from the napoluluna/bpi-wifi5-openwrt port of the
driver to Linux 6.18 (driver/0001-sf_wifi-port-to-linux-6.18.patch),
carried over to the sf19a2890-6.9 branch. That port carries no
Signed-off-by; this patch is submitted under mine.

Link: https://github.com/napoluluna/bpi-wifi5-openwrt

Signed-off-by: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
 sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_cfgfile.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_cfgfile.c
+++ b/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_cfgfile.c
@@ -426,9 +426,9 @@ int siwifi_parse_rf_gain_table_configfil
             }
             else{
                 if(siwifi_hw->mod_params->is_hb) {
-                    memcpy(&siwifi_hw->phy_config.hb_rf_gain_tb_idx[i],tb_idx,sizeof(tb_idx[0]));
+                    siwifi_hw->phy_config.hb_rf_gain_tb_idx[i] = (u8)tb_idx[0];
                 } else
-                    memcpy(&siwifi_hw->phy_config.lb_rf_gain_tb_idx[i],tb_idx,sizeof(tb_idx[0]));
+                    siwifi_hw->phy_config.lb_rf_gain_tb_idx[i] = (u8)tb_idx[0];
             }
         } else {
             if(siwifi_hw->mod_params->is_hb) {
